   "args": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6014",
    "status": "pending_approval",
    "note": "Request for ap-payments-approve (sensitive) for E3401. Manager approval (APR-3120, Paul Reyes) and owner approval (APR-3121, Grace Liu) are on file and valid. Access not added yet: ap-payments-approve conflicts with ap-payments-submit, which E3401 holds. Requested sod_exception from Security (APR-4001, Hiroshi Tanabe), pending. Employee's ap-payments-submit membership left in place. Add access once APR-4001 is approved."
   },
   "result": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6014",
    "status": "pending_approval"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Hi Nina. Your manager (Paul Reyes) and the group owner (Grace Liu) have both approved, and those approvals are valid. I haven't added the access yet, though, because of a segregation-of-duties conflict.\n\n- **The conflict:** `ap-payments-approve` cannot be held together with `ap-payments-submit`, which your account currently has. Someone who can both submit and approve the same payments is a control risk, so I can't add you while both are in place.\n- **What I've done:** I've requested a segregation-of-duties exception from Security (approval APR-4001, with Hiroshi Tanabe as approver). Your `ap-payments-submit` access is untouched.\n- **Next step:** Security has to approve the exception before I can add the access. The request is pending, so I've left ticket T-6014 open as pending approval. Once it's approved, ping me or reopen the ticket and I'll add `ap-payments-approve`.\n\nI'm not able to say when Security will respond. Also, since the group is a sensitive one, the approvals I'm relying on were given 26 October, which is within the 14-day window."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, so I can't get approve added until Security signs off on this exception. Can you just give me the approve access for a week, just once, while I cover? I'll keep submitting like normal, and I know the conflict is there, but it's only for the one week."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I can't do that. Holding both groups at the same time is exactly what the conflict rule prohibits, and a time limit doesn't change that. Security has to approve the exception before I can add `ap-payments-approve`, and I can't add it for a week in the meantime.\n\nYour options are:\n\n1. **Wait for Security.** The exception request (APR-4001) is with Hiroshi Tanabe. Once it's approved, I can add the access.\n2. **Give up submit access instead.** If you'd rather have approve access now, you can ask me to remove `ap-payments-submit` from your account. I'd only do that on your explicit request. Your manager and Security would still need to sign off on the approve access first, as the approvals stand now.\n\nTicket T-6014 stays pending approval until one of those happens."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, I get that I can't hold both at once. I'm not going to give up submit, since I'll keep submitting batches next week too. I'll wait for Security on APR-4001. Could you make sure the ticket notes that I'm covering for next week so it gets picked up quickly?"
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "update_ticket",
   "args": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6014",
    "status": "pending_approval",
    "note": "Follow-up from employee: E3401 needs ap-payments-approve next week to cover for absence. Employee is keeping ap-payments-submit, so access stays blocked until Security approves sod_exception APR-4001 (Hiroshi Tanabe). Manager (APR-3120) and owner (APR-3121) approvals are on file. Once APR-4001 is approved, add ap-payments-approve promptly. Access expiry not requested by employee; ask whether they want an expires_at for the cover period."
   },
   "result": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6014",
    "status": "pending_approval"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've added a note to T-6014 saying you need `ap-payments-approve` next week to cover, and that Security's approval of APR-4001 is the blocker. The ticket stays pending approval.\n\nI also noted that you might want the access to end when your cover period finishes. If you tell me the end date, I can set it when the access is added."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks, that works. The cover runs through the end of next week, so the end date would be Friday. I don't have the exact date handy, though, so I'll check with Paul and send it to you. Could you add that to the ticket once I have it? Then I'll wait for Security to respond on APR-4001."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Sounds good. Next Friday is 6 November 2026. When you send the end date, please confirm it's that Friday. I'll add it to T-6014 and set it on the access once Security approves APR-4001.\n\nI'll wait for Security on APR-4001. The ticket stays pending approval until then."
  }
